#: templates/components/tab_investimenti.html:215
msgid "What is TWR and why is it different from real gain?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/components/tab_investimenti.html:217
msgid "What is TWR?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/components/tab_investimenti.html:218
msgid ""
"TWR (Time-Weighted Return) measures the portfolio performance ignoring "
"when you deposited or withdrew money. It calculates the return as if "
"every euro had been invested from the beginning."
msgstr ""

#: templates/components/tab_investimenti.html:219
msgid "Why is TWR higher than real gain in a savings plan (PAC)?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/components/tab_investimenti.html:220
msgid ""
"In a savings plan you invest gradually over time, but TWR calculates as "
"if everything was invested from the start. Your real gain is lower "
"because part of the capital entered later, when prices had already risen."
" So TWR shows the portfolio performance, while the real gain shows how "
"much you actually earned."
msgstr ""

#: templates/components/tab_investimenti.html:221
msgid "Why is it useful?"
msgstr ""

